## Define a managed node

A `Rclex.LifecycleNode` is just a module that `use`s the behaviour and
overrides any callbacks it cares about. Each callback returns
`{:ok, user_state}`, `{:error, user_state}` (transition fails, stays in
previous state), or `{:fatal, user_state}` (goes to `:finalized`).

```elixir
defmodule ManagedTalker do
  use Rclex.LifecycleNode

  @impl true
  def on_configure(state) do
    IO.puts("[managed] on_configure")
    {:ok, Map.put(state, :configured, true)}
  end

  @impl true
  def on_activate(state) do
    IO.puts("[managed] on_activate — would start publishing now")
    {:ok, Map.put(state, :active, true)}
  end

  @impl true
  def on_deactivate(state) do
    IO.puts("[managed] on_deactivate")
    {:ok, Map.put(state, :active, false)}
  end

  @impl true
  def on_cleanup(state) do
    IO.puts("[managed] on_cleanup")
    {:ok, Map.delete(state, :configured)}
  end

  @impl true
  def on_shutdown(state) do
    IO.puts("[managed] on_shutdown")
    {:ok, state}
  end
end
```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```
{:module, ManagedTalker, <<70, 79, 82, 49, 0, 0, 15, ...>>, ...}
```

## Drive the state machine from the notebook

```elixir
:ok = Rclex.start_lifecycle_node(ManagedTalker, "managed_talker", user_state: %{})

IO.puts("state = #{inspect(Rclex.lifecycle_get_state("managed_talker"))}")

:ok = Rclex.lifecycle_change_state("managed_talker", :configure)
IO.puts("state = #{inspect(Rclex.lifecycle_get_state("managed_talker"))}")

:ok = Rclex.lifecycle_change_state("managed_talker", :activate)
IO.puts("state = #{inspect(Rclex.lifecycle_get_state("managed_talker"))}")
```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```
state = :unconfigured
[managed] on_configure
state = :inactive
[managed] on_activate — would start publishing now
state = :active
```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```
:ok
```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```
[managed] on_deactivate
[managed] on_cleanup
```

## Drive it from `ros2 lifecycle`

While the cell above keeps the node alive, run from another terminal:

```sh
ros2 lifecycle get /managed_talker
ros2 lifecycle set /managed_talker deactivate
ros2 lifecycle set /managed_talker cleanup
```

## Cleanup

```elixir
Rclex.stop_lifecycle_node("managed_talker")
```

